WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.242 --> 00:00:02.045
- David Oyelowo is maybe one of the most

00:00:02.045 --> 00:00:04.478
charming actors to join me on this stage.

00:00:04.478 --> 00:00:06.804
It's so easy to hang on
to every word he says,

00:00:06.804 --> 00:00:08.609
just look back at his visit here

00:00:08.609 --> 00:00:10.603
and you'll see what I mean.

00:00:10.603 --> 00:00:12.965
But is it true that your dad was a king?

00:00:12.965 --> 00:00:15.231
- Ah, well, my grandfather was a king.

00:00:15.231 --> 00:00:16.064
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:00:16.064 --> 00:00:16.897
- My dad was a-

00:00:16.897 --> 00:00:17.730
- What!?

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:18.688
- [David] Yeah, yeah.

00:00:18.688 --> 00:00:19.662
- That's so cool.

00:00:19.662 --> 00:00:20.670
- It is cool.

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:22.361
- [Kelly] Wait, or not or what? (laughs)

00:00:22.361 --> 00:00:23.194
- No, it is cool!

00:00:23.194 --> 00:00:25.542
Well, because you know,
when I was growing up,

00:00:25.542 --> 00:00:27.469
you know, I was growing up in the UK,

00:00:27.469 --> 00:00:29.488
you think of the royal family as the Queen

00:00:29.488 --> 00:00:30.321
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:00:30.321 --> 00:00:32.677
- and you know, it's Buckingham
palace and all of that.

00:00:32.677 --> 00:00:36.351
And so my dad, you know, my
dad had these tribal marks.

00:00:36.351 --> 00:00:38.204
He had four tribal marks on his face

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:40.916
and he told me that when he was younger,

00:00:40.916 --> 00:00:42.008
he fought a tiger,

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:43.724
which is why he had these tribal marks.

00:00:43.724 --> 00:00:44.602
And I thought, oh, okay.

00:00:44.602 --> 00:00:46.371
So whenever I would go to school,

00:00:46.371 --> 00:00:48.304
I'd be like, don't touch
me, don't bully me,

00:00:48.304 --> 00:00:49.945
because my dad for a tiger and survived,

00:00:49.945 --> 00:00:50.953
so don't mess with me.

00:00:50.953 --> 00:00:51.918
- (laughs) So!

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:53.285
- But he would also tell me

00:00:53.285 --> 00:00:56.274
that we were a royal
family back in Nigeria.

00:00:56.274 --> 00:00:59.496
And I was more ready
to believe in the tiger

00:00:59.496 --> 00:01:02.179
than the royal family, because
I had the royal family.

00:01:02.179 --> 00:01:04.314
I was like, there's no way
we're like the royal family!

00:01:04.314 --> 00:01:07.383
So we then moved back to
Nigeria when I was about six

00:01:07.383 --> 00:01:11.404
and all my relatives came to
pick us up from the airport

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:15.153
and all the men had
apparently fought a tiger.

00:01:15.153 --> 00:01:17.076
(David, Kelly, and audience laughs)

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:21.959
- So I was like, but dad, are
there even tigers in Nigeria?

00:01:21.959 --> 00:01:24.799
But weirdly that was the lie.

00:01:24.799 --> 00:01:25.682
- [Kelly] Lies!

00:01:25.682 --> 00:01:27.286
- The truth was that we were actually all

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:30.982
from a royal family and we
lived on Oyelowo street,

00:01:30.982 --> 00:01:33.232
and my family and all them.

00:01:34.335 --> 00:01:35.168
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:01:35.168 --> 00:01:36.611
Part of Western Nigeria called Awe

00:01:36.611 --> 00:01:38.957
is where we are the royal family of.

00:01:38.957 --> 00:01:40.614
- That is so cool!

00:01:40.614 --> 00:01:41.777
(audience clapping)

00:01:41.777 --> 00:01:44.064
We also got to talking
about David's life at home

00:01:44.064 --> 00:01:45.605
and he is quite the family man.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.010
Here's something we've never shown before.

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:49.749
Are any of your kids driving yet?

00:01:49.749 --> 00:01:50.672
Are you terrified?

00:01:50.672 --> 00:01:52.827
By the way, your family is beautiful!

00:01:52.827 --> 00:01:53.660
- [David] Thank you.

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:56.442
- You're like the family in the
photos when you buy a frame.

00:01:56.442 --> 00:01:58.460
(everyone laughs)

00:01:58.460 --> 00:01:59.718
It's unreal.

00:01:59.718 --> 00:02:02.139
- Maybe we should do
that, like a side hustle.

00:02:02.139 --> 00:02:02.998
- I'm just saying, yeah.

00:02:02.998 --> 00:02:05.819
If it doesn't work out, there's your job.

00:02:05.819 --> 00:02:07.783
- Exactly. Thank you.
Thank you for saying that.

00:02:07.783 --> 00:02:09.365
Yeah, my eldest son is now 19.

00:02:09.365 --> 00:02:11.975
He does drive. He's a
very responsible driver.

00:02:11.975 --> 00:02:12.808
- [Kelly] Oh!

00:02:12.808 --> 00:02:16.649
- But my second son is
15 and that's Caleb.

00:02:16.649 --> 00:02:18.403
Oh, there he is. (laughs)

00:02:18.403 --> 00:02:20.378
You can tell, yeah, the one
giving you the peace sign.

00:02:20.378 --> 00:02:21.211
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:02:21.211 --> 00:02:22.442
= That's my 15 year old Caleb.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:26.845
He's the one I'm a little
bit more concerned about.

00:02:26.845 --> 00:02:28.770
- I mean, from the photo,
I would be too. (laughs)

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:29.603
- [David] Yeah, exactly.

00:02:29.603 --> 00:02:31.061
- He's someone fun, like playful.

00:02:31.061 --> 00:02:32.170
- He has a talent for breaking things.

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:33.016
- [Kelly] Ah.

00:02:33.016 --> 00:02:34.490
- You know, things, himself.

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:35.570
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:38.577
- And so we have decided
that he has got to go

00:02:38.577 --> 00:02:41.386
a full year without breaking anything

00:02:41.386 --> 00:02:43.732
before he's allowed to drive.

00:02:43.732 --> 00:02:45.375
- Oh my God, you definitely
break a lot of things

00:02:45.375 --> 00:02:47.169
when that's a rule.

00:02:47.169 --> 00:02:48.418
- Yeah, well, exactly.

00:02:48.418 --> 00:02:51.293
And we don't want him breaking
himself or the car, in a car.

00:02:51.293 --> 00:02:55.011
And so that's why we've
decided to do that.

00:02:55.011 --> 00:02:57.606
So he keeps on, he keeps
on shifting (chuckles)

00:02:57.606 --> 00:02:59.312
- [Kelly] He's never going to drive.

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:00.602
- Because he keeps on breaking things.

00:03:00.602 --> 00:03:02.261
- He was like, whatever. I'll Uber.

00:03:02.261 --> 00:03:04.397
Do you, quick question from that picture,

00:03:04.397 --> 00:03:07.359
do you all just get together and work out?

00:03:07.359 --> 00:03:09.231
(everyone laughs)

00:03:09.231 --> 00:03:10.420
Like I just saw that picture

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:12.719
and this wasn't even
supposed to be a question,

00:03:12.719 --> 00:03:15.449
but I was like, what do
y'all do, workouts together?

00:03:15.449 --> 00:03:18.678
Like, you're all like very fit.

00:03:18.678 --> 00:03:19.984
- We actually do.

00:03:19.984 --> 00:03:23.002
We're blessed enough
to have a gym at home.

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.364
- I have a gym at home!

00:03:24.364 --> 00:03:25.491
- (chuckling) Oh, really?

00:03:25.491 --> 00:03:27.683
- I have a gym at home, okay?

00:03:27.683 --> 00:03:30.983
Not everybody with a gym
at home looks like that.

00:03:30.983 --> 00:03:32.784
(everyone continues laughing)

00:03:32.784 --> 00:03:35.767
I'm just saying that
doesn't always pan out.

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:37.600
So what's your secret?

00:03:38.709 --> 00:03:40.130
- Oh, man. Well, I don't know.

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:44.222
As an actor, I sort of think
of actors as athletes as well.

00:03:44.222 --> 00:03:46.254
I have to change my body a lot.

00:03:46.254 --> 00:03:47.581
- Oh, that's why I can
never be an actor. (laughs)

00:03:47.581 --> 00:03:48.414
- [David] Ah, see. There you go.

00:03:48.414 --> 00:03:49.247
- It's not for me.

00:03:49.247 --> 00:03:50.948
- [David] You could be. I
could see you doing that.

00:03:50.948 --> 00:03:51.936
No, actually in the Midnight Sky,

00:03:51.936 --> 00:03:54.243
I had to do about three
months of training.

00:03:54.243 --> 00:03:55.134
- [Kelly] Wow!

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:57.831
- For all the spacewalk stuff,

00:03:57.831 --> 00:04:00.081
because you had to get a very strong core

00:04:00.081 --> 00:04:01.632
because it's all wire work.

00:04:01.632 --> 00:04:03.590
And in order to look like you're floating,

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.161
you actually have to, you know,

00:04:05.161 --> 00:04:07.977
really be employing a lot of effort.

00:04:07.977 --> 00:04:10.543
- I just pictured me doing
it. (everyone laughs)

00:04:10.543 --> 00:04:12.193
It wasn't as graceful.

00:04:12.193 --> 00:04:14.799
- It's really painful, the
harness is right up in here

00:04:14.799 --> 00:04:16.853
so I'm glad I had my four kids first.

00:04:16.853 --> 00:04:18.493
- [Kelly] Yeah. You
should try Spanx, my man.

00:04:18.493 --> 00:04:19.326
(everyone laughs)

00:04:19.326 --> 00:04:21.191
I'm used to tight there.

00:04:21.191 --> 00:04:23.765
Is it true that you kept chickens at home?

00:04:23.765 --> 00:04:24.598
- I do!

00:04:24.598 --> 00:04:26.452
- [Kelly] I had chickens
when I was in Tennessee.

00:04:26.452 --> 00:04:28.585
I don't have them here,
but do you love it?

00:04:28.585 --> 00:04:29.437
Y'all love it?

00:04:29.437 --> 00:04:30.470
- Yeah, they provide eggs.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:31.303
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:04:31.303 --> 00:04:32.906
They provide entertainment.

00:04:32.906 --> 00:04:33.759
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:33.759 --> 00:04:35.641
We got them at the
beginning of the pandemic.

00:04:35.641 --> 00:04:37.808
We thought, okay, let's
get closer to the earth.

00:04:37.808 --> 00:04:38.641
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:38.641 --> 00:04:40.722
- And we now have every form of egg,

00:04:40.722 --> 00:04:43.043
omelet, scrambled egg, anything.

00:04:43.043 --> 00:04:43.943
- [Kelly] I love it!

00:04:43.943 --> 00:04:45.741
- We now know everything
you can do with an egg.

00:04:45.741 --> 00:04:46.637
(audience laughs)

00:04:46.637 --> 00:04:47.470
- Yes, same thing.

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:51.117
I love the fact that you're
self-sustaining as well.

00:04:51.117 --> 00:04:52.103
That's cool.

00:04:52.103 --> 00:04:53.978
- Yeah, yeah, yeah. Makes
you feel like a man!

00:04:53.978 --> 00:04:55.010
Collecting eggs.

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:56.154
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:04:56.154 --> 00:04:57.650
- [Kelly] Yeah. I am like
the people back then.

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:59.234
I can do everything. I'm
a gatherer and hunter.

00:04:59.234 --> 00:05:00.067
- [David] Yeah, exactly.

00:05:00.067 --> 00:05:01.408
- Well, I think we have a little video

00:05:01.408 --> 00:05:02.547
of you with your chickens.

00:05:02.547 --> 00:05:04.003
- [David] Oh yeah, I
did the video for you.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.325
- Yes.

00:05:05.325 --> 00:05:06.542
- Okay, so as promised,

00:05:06.542 --> 00:05:08.525
I'm going to introduce you to my chickens.

00:05:08.525 --> 00:05:11.463
They all have interesting names.

00:05:11.463 --> 00:05:13.453
That's Slough.

00:05:13.453 --> 00:05:14.630
(audience laughs)

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:17.399
I think that's Potato, that's Star.

00:05:17.399 --> 00:05:18.982
That's Aubergine...

00:05:22.051 --> 00:05:23.717
and that's Rona.

00:05:23.717 --> 00:05:24.620
(audience laughs)

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:27.299
And then one of them is
called Untitled Project.

00:05:27.299 --> 00:05:30.299
(everyone laughing)

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:33.167
- Untitled Project, you're awesome.

